@@ -32,6 +32,25 @@

 The reminder does not fold anything itself. The agent chooses what to fold and writes the summaries.

+## Configuration
+
+Automatic context-maintenance nudges are enabled by default. To disable them,
+create `<Pi agent dir>/extensions/infinite-context.json` (normally
+`~/.pi/agent/extensions/infinite-context.json`):
+
+```json
+{
+  "enableNudges": false
+}
+```
+
+The global setting is read at session start (or the first turn in headless hosts
+that omit that event). It only disables the agent-facing reminder. All five
+tools, their results/errors, and native-compaction blocking and warnings for
+manual, threshold, and overflow compaction remain unchanged. Missing or invalid
+config defaults to enabled. Disable these nudges when another extension such as
+`context-pressure` owns reminders.
+
 ## Limits

 This extension does not enlarge the model's context window. Summaries can leave out details; the agent may need to find them in the archive later.
